  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let, $x^2+y^2=16$ or $x^2+y^2=4^2$ radius of circle $r_1=4$, centre $\\mathrm{C}_1(0,0)$ we have, $x^2+y^2-2 y=0$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\Rightarrow & x^2+\\left(y^2-2 y+1\\right)-1=0 \\text { or } x^2+(y-1)^2 \\\\\n=& 1^2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nRadius 1, centre $\\mathrm{C}_2(0,1)$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\left|C_1 C_2\\right|=1 \\\\\n&\\left|r_2-r_1\\right|=|4-1|=3 \\\\\n&\\left|C_1 C_2\\right| < \\left|r_2-r_1\\right|\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nno common tangents for these two circles.",
    "image": null
  },
